    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0460" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg440"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 71.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 14, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge, with much
                    satisfaction, the receipt of your despatch of June, (No. 82,) in which you
                    inform me that the Chinese government has agreed to the principle of the joint
                    tribunal or mixed commission for the settlement of confiscation cases.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq.,<hi
                            rendition="#italic"> &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
